{"name":"War Paint Red","hex":"#dc571d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"war","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Waray-Waray."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Organized, large-scale, armed conflict between countries or between national, ethnic, or other sizeable groups, usually but not always involving active engagement of military forces.(Can we clean up this sense?)","A particular conflict of this kind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/war"},{"term":"paint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substance that is applied as a liquid or paste, and dries into a solid coating that protects or adds colour to an object or surface to which it has been applied.","A set of containers or blocks of paint of different colors/colours, used for painting pictures."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply paint to.","To apply in the manner that paint is applied."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paint"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"War","blocks":[{"text":"War is an armed conflict between the armed forces of states, or between governmental forces and armed groups that are organized under a certain command structure and have the capacity to sustain military operations, or between such organized groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Stele_of_Vultures_detail_01a.jpg/330px-Stele_of_Vultures_detail_01a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War","wikidata":"Q198"},{"title":"Paint","blocks":[{"text":"Paint is a material or mixture of colored liquid that, when applied to a solid material and allowed to dry, adds a film-like layer. As art, this is used to create an image or images known as a painting. Paint can be made in many colors and types. Most paints are either oil-based or water-based, and each has distinct characteristics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Multicolored_tempera_paints.jpg/330px-Multicolored_tempera_paints.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paint","wikidata":"Q174219"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Bayeuxtapestryscene52.jpg/500px-Bayeuxtapestryscene52.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Bayeuxtapestryscene52.jpg/1280px-Bayeuxtapestryscene52.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thum